{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "AgentCI Guard",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/David-Wu1119/agentci-guard",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "agentci/gated-ai-write-token",
              "name": "Untrusted event content reaches a write-capable agent that gates on repository write access",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Untrusted event content reaches a write-capable agent that gates on repository write access"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The untrusted-trigger, AI-agent, write-token pattern is present, but the agent is anthropics/claude-code-action, which by default refuses to run for users without repository write access, so a stranger's issue or comment does not reach the agent as configured. Two residual risks remain: a user with write access can act on attacker-authored content (a maintainer @-mentioning the agent on a malicious issue), and the check lives inside the action at runtime, where a bypass was disclosed in January 2026. One configuration change makes this critical."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Keep the default gate: never set allowed_non_write_users, and avoid allowed_bots. Pin the action to a commit SHA so a fixed authorization check cannot silently regress. Prefer read-only permissions on untrusted triggers and move writes to a separate, maintainer-approved job. Treat maintainer @-mentions on untrusted issues as a review step, not an automation trigger.",
                "markdown": "- Keep the default gate: never set allowed_non_write_users, and avoid allowed_bots.\n- Pin the action to a commit SHA so a fixed authorization check cannot silently regress.\n- Prefer read-only permissions on untrusted triggers and move writes to a separate, maintainer-approved job.\n- Treat maintainer @-mentions on untrusted issues as a review step, not an automation trigger."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "agentci/ai-with-secrets",
              "name": "AI agent job has access to secrets",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "AI agent job has access to secrets"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Secrets mounted into an AI-agent job can be exfiltrated if untrusted prompt content influences tool use, shell commands, or generated output. Most AI actions require a provider key, so this is a baseline exposure to review rather than a vulnerability on its own — it becomes high-risk when combined with untrusted input or write permissions (see agentci/untrusted-ai-write-token)."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Do not expose secrets to agent jobs that process untrusted content. Use short-lived scoped tokens. Move secret-bearing actions behind manual approval.",
                "markdown": "- Do not expose secrets to agent jobs that process untrusted content.\n- Use short-lived scoped tokens.\n- Move secret-bearing actions behind manual approval."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "agentci/broad-write-permissions",
              "name": "Workflow grants broad write permissions near AI usage",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Workflow grants broad write permissions near AI usage"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Broad write scopes increase blast radius if an AI-agent step is influenced by untrusted input."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Set default permissions to read-only. Grant write scopes only in narrowly scoped jobs. Prefer job-level permissions over workflow-level write permissions.",
                "markdown": "- Set default permissions to read-only.\n- Grant write scopes only in narrowly scoped jobs.\n- Prefer job-level permissions over workflow-level write permissions."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "agentci/gated-ai-write-token",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Untrusted event content reaches a write-capable agent that gates on repository write access: untrusted trigger + AI usage + effective write permission, but anthropics/claude-code-action refuses users without repository write access by default; no allowed_non_write_users / allowed_bots bypass, no pull_request_target or discussion trigger, no untrusted text in a run: step. Residual: a write-access user acting on attacker content, and any bypass in the action's own check."
          },
          "properties": {
            "agentci/severity": "high",
            "agentci/reachableEvents": [
              "issue_comment",
              "issues",
              "pull_request_review",
              "pull_request_review_comment"
            ],
            "agentci/job": "claude"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": ".github/workflows/claude.yml"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 14
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "agentci/ai-with-secrets",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "AI agent job has access to secrets: AI step's effective environment or inputs reference a secret/token"
          },
          "properties": {
            "agentci/severity": "medium",
            "agentci/reachableEvents": [
              "issue_comment",
              "issues",
              "pull_request_review",
              "pull_request_review_comment"
            ],
            "agentci/job": "claude"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": ".github/workflows/claude.yml"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 14
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "agentci/broad-write-permissions",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Workflow grants broad write permissions near AI usage: effective permissions: {\"source\":\"job\",\"default\":\"none\",\"scopes\":{\"contents\":\"write\",\"pull-requests\":\"write\",\"issues\":\"write\",\"id-token\":\"write\",\"actions\":\"read\"}}"
          },
          "properties": {
            "agentci/severity": "medium",
            "agentci/reachableEvents": [
              "issue_comment",
              "issues",
              "pull_request_review",
              "pull_request_review_comment"
            ],
            "agentci/job": "claude"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": ".github/workflows/claude.yml"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 14
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": false,
          "toolExecutionNotifications": [
            {
              "descriptor": {
                "id": "agentci/analysis-event-condition"
              },
              "level": "warning",
              "message": {
                "text": "Could not fully interpret this job's github.event_name condition; event reachability was kept conservative."
              },
              "locations": [
                {
                  "physicalLocation": {
                    "artifactLocation": {
                      "uri": ".github/workflows/claude.yml"
                    },
                    "region": {
                      "startLine": 14
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "properties": {
                "agentci/kind": "analysis",
                "agentci/job": "claude"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "properties": {
        "agentci/analysisComplete": false,
        "agentci/diagnosticCount": 1
      }
    }
  ]
}
